WEBVTT

00:00.390 --> 00:06.400
<b>Look with your own eyes, and it should be obvious:</b>

00:00.490 --> 00:04.620
Look with your own eyes,
and it should be obvious:

00:04.620 --> 00:09.140
It's actually quite easy to
become an excellent detective.

00:06.400 --> 00:09.150
<b>It's actually quite easy to become an excellent detective</b>

00:23.360 --> 00:24.890
Hurry up, mister so-called
excellent detective!

00:24.890 --> 00:25.620
We're getting out of here!

00:25.620 --> 00:27.540
Hey, Minoura-kun.

00:27.540 --> 00:29.350
That took you a while.

00:29.900 --> 00:35.210
I hate to admit you predicted all this, 
but either way, I'm here to help.

00:35.210 --> 00:36.090
Why?

00:38.630 --> 00:39.980
I did what you said.

00:40.220 --> 00:42.600
I trusted my soul.

00:44.050 --> 00:45.370
Surrender!

00:45.370 --> 00:47.120
You're surrounded!

00:48.220 --> 00:50.570
Wretched terrorists...

00:50.570 --> 00:52.180
You're done now.

00:52.530 --> 00:54.220
Say, mister excellent detective...

00:54.900 --> 00:58.540
You're right. The police 
of this nation are idiots.

00:58.540 --> 01:01.130
But not all of us.

01:05.080 --> 01:06.780
What are you doing?!

01:06.780 --> 01:09.080
We're following our guts!

01:09.080 --> 01:10.210
Protect the detective!

01:14.560 --> 01:16.990
Do you have any idea what you've done?

01:16.990 --> 01:19.450
You've split the police force into two!

01:19.450 --> 01:20.830
Yup, that's right.

01:21.370 --> 01:24.520
I split them into the correct police 
and the misguided police.

01:24.990 --> 01:28.950
So you knew that some number of officers 
would trust your righteousness and intellect

01:28.950 --> 01:32.610
and throw down their lives for you?

01:34.560 --> 01:35.570
Actually...

01:36.340 --> 01:38.810
I had no way of knowing if they'd believe me.

01:43.130 --> 01:44.780
Well, shit.

01:45.560 --> 01:47.940
Turns out you're quite the idiot, too.

03:26.950 --> 03:28.550
He's all yours, Kunikida.

03:31.300 --> 03:33.570
Oh, dear. Look how happy he is.

03:33.950 --> 03:35.790
I guess I can't blame him.

03:35.790 --> 03:37.840
He's been struggling all on his own.

03:38.710 --> 03:41.210
You can go in for the hug, too.

03:41.210 --> 03:42.720
I'm holding back.

03:45.080 --> 03:46.150
Kunikida-san!

03:46.430 --> 03:47.610
Your hands!

03:47.610 --> 03:49.230
Relax.

03:50.020 --> 03:51.530
I'll take care of it.

03:53.490 --> 03:56.500
That's the whole point of having 
the whole Agency back together.

03:58.090 --> 04:00.510
Yosano-san is here for us when we're injured.

04:00.510 --> 04:02.870
Rampo-san is here for us when 
we're captured by the enemy.

04:03.610 --> 04:06.090
This organization, the Detective Agency,

04:06.550 --> 04:09.400
brings out strengths in us we could
 never access on our own.

04:09.400 --> 04:10.310
Right.

04:10.660 --> 04:12.860
The enemy knew that, too,

04:12.860 --> 04:16.310
which is why they caused the incident right 
as the Agency members were split up.

04:17.370 --> 04:21.280
They aren't going to get their 
way anymore, though, are they?

04:21.280 --> 04:23.620
It's not over yet.

04:24.250 --> 04:26.690
You two, look for Kenji and Tanizaki.

04:27.450 --> 04:28.380
What will you do?

04:29.220 --> 04:31.080
What do you think?

04:31.080 --> 04:34.580
Episode 52

04:31.080 --> 04:34.580
<b><i>The Answer to Everything</i></b>

04:31.380 --> 04:34.310
I'm doing the funnest part of the job.

04:36.030 --> 04:37.320
Fukuchi-dono!

04:38.510 --> 04:41.750
On behalf of the United Nations,
I'm begging you...

04:42.230 --> 04:47.130
Please help us build our 
counter-terrorism organization.

04:49.860 --> 04:52.430
Why won't he say anything?

04:52.430 --> 04:56.400
Is he offended by our disrespectful request?

05:00.400 --> 05:02.900
<b>Blorgh</b>

05:03.710 --> 05:05.290
A hangover?

05:05.290 --> 05:06.170
Indeed.

05:06.480 --> 05:12.030
Last night, he opened two bottles of Tyrant, 
and then proceeded to go barhopping.

05:12.410 --> 05:15.040
If not for the tamagozake I prepared for him,

05:15.320 --> 05:20.440
he would have been unable to speak,
let alone attend.

05:20.440 --> 05:26.430
To be honest, I think half of my nausea 
is because of that tamagozake.

05:26.430 --> 05:28.060
What kind of egg did you make it with, anyway?

05:28.370 --> 05:29.590
Frog eggs.

05:32.470 --> 05:34.930
<b>Blorf</b>

05:35.920 --> 05:37.820
Holy smokes, that was rough.

05:38.350 --> 05:40.820
I was seeing an entire 
galaxy's worth of stars.

05:41.370 --> 05:43.840
Oh, please, have a seat.

05:44.360 --> 05:49.400
Fukuchi-dono, have you had a chance to 
consider the matter we contacted you about?

05:51.400 --> 05:53.610
The establishment of a 
counter-terrorism organization?

05:54.960 --> 05:59.450
Fukuchi-dono, when do you 
suppose a life ends?

05:59.810 --> 06:03.500
It's when it becomes unable 
to adapt to change.

06:03.500 --> 06:07.440
Like the dinosaurs who were wiped out by the 
climate change caused by a meteorite impact,

06:08.300 --> 06:12.070
the world is on the brink of 
being changed by terrorism.

06:12.550 --> 06:17.160
If your Hunting Dogs hadn't intervened 
during the Sky Casino incident,

06:17.160 --> 06:19.470
the world may well have ended.

06:19.720 --> 06:20.680
And?

06:21.470 --> 06:24.110
We will unite justice throughout the world.

06:24.720 --> 06:26.620
They will be unaffiliated with any nation.

06:26.620 --> 06:29.070
They will be free of any baggage.

06:29.070 --> 06:32.420
A military police force with
the entire planet as its jurisdiction.

06:32.420 --> 06:35.010
That is what we will create.

06:35.010 --> 06:37.900
Dreams are always beautiful, aren't they?

06:37.900 --> 06:40.960
No, this is no dream.

06:40.960 --> 06:43.650
We even have a special weapon to that end.

06:43.650 --> 06:45.220
A special weapon?

06:45.450 --> 06:46.760
You.

06:47.080 --> 06:50.110
You must command that army.

06:50.110 --> 06:54.360
Let us begin by destroying the 
Armed Detective Agency terrorist group.

06:55.380 --> 06:56.710
I don't like it.

06:56.710 --> 06:58.700
H-How so?

06:58.700 --> 07:02.020
If there's anything you disagree with,
we can readjust.

07:02.020 --> 07:04.190
The Detective Agency? Terrorists?

07:04.190 --> 07:06.760
Are you still spouting such nonsense?

07:07.490 --> 07:11.030
I wouldn't mind taking on the project,
 but on one condition.

07:11.480 --> 07:14.610
I'll have the priorities of the 
investigation changed.

07:13.200 --> 07:16.950
<b>Standard
Mechanical
Island</b>

07:18.200 --> 07:22.330
That concludes my description of the 
Supernational Armed Security Force.

07:22.770 --> 07:24.580
We are at war.

07:24.580 --> 07:27.960
Our war against terrorists 
has already begun.

07:27.960 --> 07:30.380
I ask for your vote in favor.

07:33.130 --> 07:35.620
A borderless counter-terrorist army?

07:35.620 --> 07:36.360
Ridiculous.

07:36.360 --> 07:38.040
They could never make it work.

07:38.340 --> 07:39.350
This is nonsense.

07:39.350 --> 07:42.680
Nothing but an excuse to pad the 
pockets of military industries.

07:42.680 --> 07:45.110
We're better off protecting our own nations.

07:50.440 --> 07:56.950
Please join me, everyone, in welcoming 
the commander of the new organization.

08:11.870 --> 08:13.330
No... It can't be.

08:13.330 --> 08:14.360
It's really him.

08:14.360 --> 08:16.510
The real Fukuchi Ouchi.

08:16.510 --> 08:18.300
Such presence!

08:18.300 --> 08:19.540
Magnificent!

08:19.540 --> 08:20.770
I'm so moved!

08:20.770 --> 08:25.000
To think I'd be breathing the 
same air as that legend of a man!

08:25.000 --> 08:27.770
It's thanks to you that we are all alive.

08:27.990 --> 08:31.500
Thanks to the work of the legendary samurai!

08:31.490 --> 08:32.990
<b>Adapted into three films!</b>

08:31.490 --> 08:32.990
<b>Adapted into three films!</b>

08:32.990 --> 08:35.610
Those films are heavily dramatized.

08:35.610 --> 08:38.900
The people here are all 
versed in defense secrets.

08:38.900 --> 08:42.780
We are all aware that your service 
is more than mere fairy tales.

08:43.300 --> 08:46.010
The elimination of hundreds 
of thousands of subjects

08:46.010 --> 08:48.620
of the werecreature experiments 
in the Republic of Kenia.

08:49.000 --> 08:52.760
The prevention of the migrant massacre at 
the hands of the Amil regime in Africa.

08:53.180 --> 08:57.280
And the prevention of the spread of the 
vampire contagion in Eastern Europe.

08:57.540 --> 09:03.020
Any one of these could have 
disrupted the world order.

09:03.350 --> 09:07.270
The world owes you more
 than it could ever repay.

09:08.320 --> 09:12.510
Then may I ask for just 
three minutes of your time?

09:12.510 --> 09:13.750
Of course.

09:14.250 --> 09:15.790
But first...

09:15.790 --> 09:17.570
Please autograph this!

09:17.570 --> 09:18.930
For me, too!

09:18.930 --> 09:20.860
May I take a photo with you?

09:24.900 --> 09:28.620
At first, I declined to be involved

09:28.620 --> 09:32.470
in establishing a 
defense force for humanity,

09:33.360 --> 09:37.480
because I was hungover and could hardly 
make sense of what was being said to me.

09:37.860 --> 09:40.130
He wasn't listening?

09:40.130 --> 09:42.920
So, why am I standing here now?

09:43.350 --> 09:47.470
Partly because the medication from 
the pharmacy was so effective.

09:49.840 --> 09:56.060
And partly because humanity 
will be doomed otherwise.

09:57.380 --> 10:00.020
We are already losing.

10:00.490 --> 10:03.760
You don't appear to have even 
considered the possibility

10:03.760 --> 10:09.620
that some of your plentiful wallets are,
in fact, filled with bombs.

10:10.830 --> 10:15.100
Our existing frameworks can no longer 
protect the safety of the world.

10:15.100 --> 10:19.290
Technological progress and the application 
of special abilities in crime;

10:19.640 --> 10:24.410
these are the two forces bringing 
about never-before-seen evil.

10:24.870 --> 10:27.580
What will you be doing on the eve of 
the world's destruction at the hands

10:27.580 --> 10:31.800
of the new-age terrorist organization 
that is the Decay of Angels?

10:31.800 --> 10:35.240
Will you spend your last 
moments enjoying a feast?

10:35.570 --> 10:36.520
No!

10:36.900 --> 10:38.440
You will resist!

10:38.440 --> 10:43.570
The people have chosen you to represent 
them because of your abilities!

10:43.800 --> 10:45.280
Am I mistaken?

10:45.640 --> 10:46.450
He's right.

10:47.170 --> 10:48.640
That's right!

10:48.640 --> 10:52.780
Terrorism in this new age calls for 
a brand new kind of organization.

10:53.160 --> 10:58.020
The chairperson has called this organization 
the Supernational Armed Security Force.

10:58.860 --> 11:02.090
But that's rather, well...

11:02.830 --> 11:03.790
Lame.

11:04.490 --> 11:07.510
I've already given it another name.

11:08.740 --> 11:10.340
The Army of Mankind.

11:10.760 --> 11:13.620
A spear against the evils of this world!

11:17.540 --> 11:23.220
I look forward to your yes vote 
on the coming resolution.

11:29.980 --> 11:31.550
Heya!

11:31.860 --> 11:35.570
I'm that terrorist everyone's talking about.

11:38.020 --> 11:40.690
The phone's right there
 if you're gonna report me.

11:46.890 --> 11:47.930
Security?

11:48.570 --> 11:50.750
Don't let anyone in for 
the next five minutes.

11:50.750 --> 11:51.800
Five minutes?

11:52.220 --> 11:53.310
That's right.

11:53.820 --> 11:55.900
Do you need more time to convince me?

11:55.900 --> 11:57.400
Of course not.

11:57.400 --> 11:58.650
It'll be easy.

12:08.510 --> 12:10.320
It's been a while, huh?

12:10.860 --> 12:13.430
You haven't changed at all, boy.

12:13.430 --> 12:16.070
You're almost the same as 
the first time I met you.

12:16.600 --> 12:21.450
That was at the Detective Agency's 
founding ceremony, wasn't it?

12:21.450 --> 12:23.840
That was such a mess.

12:23.840 --> 12:27.260
You came in drunk, 
made a huge mess of the venue,

12:27.260 --> 12:30.530
and peed on the brand new Agency banner.

12:30.530 --> 12:31.750
That was...

12:31.750 --> 12:32.700
Sorry.

12:32.700 --> 12:34.130
I apologize for that.

12:34.130 --> 12:37.150
After that, the president told me...

12:37.590 --> 12:39.960
Gen'ichiro and I go way back.

12:39.960 --> 12:42.620
I trust that man more than anyone.

12:43.040 --> 12:47.310
He must be a little lonely,
now that I've found my own path.

12:47.910 --> 12:48.910
That's what he said.

12:49.400 --> 12:52.500
What could I do after the 
president told me that?

12:55.190 --> 12:59.830
I came here because the president 
asked me to meet you.

13:00.310 --> 13:04.460
The Decay of Angels is intent on 
destroying the state in six days.

13:04.800 --> 13:09.110
Before that, we need to defeat their 
leader, Kamui, and retrieve the page.

13:09.530 --> 13:13.650
To that end, as the man who has the
 whole world on his side, I need your help.

13:14.050 --> 13:15.620
That's why I'm joining forces with you.

13:16.070 --> 13:18.240
That's the only way we can defeat them.

13:19.000 --> 13:20.700
I see.

13:20.700 --> 13:24.020
I thought it was odd that 
you hadn't shown up yet.

13:24.020 --> 13:27.210
You were waiting for the 
speech today, weren't you?

13:27.210 --> 13:29.230
You can think what you'd like.

13:29.230 --> 13:30.840
Well? What's your answer?

13:30.840 --> 13:32.800
Yes or no?

13:33.800 --> 13:39.330
Have you let your self-proclaimed title of 
"excellent detective" get to your head?

13:39.330 --> 13:44.470
I was expecting you'd have the rhetoric 
to sway me at least a little.

13:45.060 --> 13:48.280
How are you so certain that I won't 
strike you down on the spot,

13:48.280 --> 13:50.800
having come armed merely 
with a plea to be believed?

13:51.140 --> 13:52.920
I'm not certain at all.

13:53.690 --> 13:57.630
I <i>could</i> completely deduce your response,

13:58.070 --> 13:59.380
but I won't.

13:59.980 --> 14:04.460
I could psychologically manipulate 
you into cooperating with me,

14:05.030 --> 14:06.610
but I won't.

14:06.900 --> 14:09.110
All I'll do is trust,

14:09.500 --> 14:12.130
because the president said quite simply...

14:13.990 --> 14:15.810
I trust Fukuchi.

14:16.770 --> 14:18.240
And nothing else.

14:19.140 --> 14:26.800
You may be guided by justice,
but I'm guided by the president.

14:27.580 --> 14:30.510
That's why I trust you, too.

14:37.350 --> 14:39.770
Fukuzawa's found some great men for himself.

14:41.330 --> 14:43.530
Well, what's the plan?

14:44.150 --> 14:47.400
<b>VIP
Guest Ship
Boswellian</b>

14:44.510 --> 14:46.650
First, we leave the island.

14:51.360 --> 14:53.440
You were able to convince him?

14:53.870 --> 14:55.020
<i>Of course!</i>

14:55.390 --> 14:56.850
Are you prepared for the smuggling?

14:56.850 --> 14:58.170
<i>As you asked.</i>

14:58.500 --> 15:00.200
<i>There is no surveillance in the area.</i>

15:00.200 --> 15:01.530
<i>We're ready to board.</i>

15:01.530 --> 15:02.610
All right!

15:08.100 --> 15:10.090
<i>That's Fukuchi Ouchi...</i>

15:10.640 --> 15:14.890
<i>The leader of the Hunting Dogs, 
synonymous with world justice.</i>

15:15.480 --> 15:18.750
<i>The Detective Agency's future hinges 
on whether he's on our side or not.</i>

15:19.080 --> 15:21.210
<i>We have to be careful not to offend him.</i>

15:25.080 --> 15:27.430
What's with that sad sit?!

15:27.430 --> 15:29.170
We don't want to get caught.

15:29.170 --> 15:30.460
Hurry up and hide with us!

15:30.460 --> 15:31.510
No way!

15:31.510 --> 15:35.070
They call you a hero, but you're 
just a lame, middle-aged man.

15:35.880 --> 15:38.940
The guards on the ship are state 
police from all over the world.

15:38.940 --> 15:42.130
If they see a criminal, 
they'll shoot on sight.

15:42.130 --> 15:44.330
Also, don't call me a middle-aged man!

15:44.890 --> 15:46.030
You are middle-aged, though.

15:46.580 --> 15:47.930
I'm still young!

15:49.610 --> 15:51.000
Come on, Rampo-san!

15:51.000 --> 15:53.060
He's a precious ally!

15:53.060 --> 15:54.950
Couldn't you be more 
careful with your words?

15:54.950 --> 15:56.690
It's fine.

15:56.690 --> 15:58.890
This boy is just jealous.

15:59.440 --> 16:02.560
It's been thirteen years 
since the boy met Fukuzawa.

16:02.560 --> 16:06.780
That's still not even half the time 
Fukuzawa and I have known each other.

16:06.780 --> 16:08.660
He's jealous of that fact.

16:09.070 --> 16:12.040
He's upset that he can't surpass me.

16:12.040 --> 16:14.120
I don't remember anything about that.

16:15.550 --> 16:18.530
With your memory? There's no way.

16:18.530 --> 16:20.130
Also, stop calling me boy!

16:20.370 --> 16:21.900
But you're a boy, boy.

16:21.040 --> 16:23.610
<i>I've never seen this side of Rampo-san.</i>

16:21.900 --> 16:22.280
Shut up!

16:22.280 --> 16:23.820
Shut up! Shut up!

16:26.640 --> 16:30.800
Who is Kamui, this grand mastermind?

16:32.430 --> 16:33.990
Slow down.

16:33.990 --> 16:39.120
This isn't like a murder case, where it's 
over as soon as we know who did it.

16:39.120 --> 16:40.970
We have to be cautious.

16:40.970 --> 16:44.060
But you have that thing, don't you?

16:46.330 --> 16:49.900
Are you trying to get me to show you <i>this?</i>

16:49.900 --> 16:51.670
I dunno...

16:51.670 --> 16:54.290
I'm getting thirsty.

16:56.060 --> 16:57.030
Here.

16:56.370 --> 16:58.580
<b>Ramune</b>

16:57.440 --> 16:58.570
This is what you want, right?

16:57.910 --> 16:58.580
<b>Bribe</b>

16:58.960 --> 17:01.010
Do you walk around with that?

17:01.010 --> 17:01.780
Yes.

17:02.130 --> 17:04.840
Whenever I work with Rampo-san.
Just in case.

17:05.400 --> 17:06.550
<b><i>Phew!</i></b>

17:06.950 --> 17:08.850
Oh, all right.

17:08.850 --> 17:10.510
Don't tell the president.

17:10.780 --> 17:12.740
<i>Rampo-san's Ultra Deduction!</i>

17:13.470 --> 17:15.930
<i>We'll finally know who Kamui is.</i>

17:17.430 --> 17:18.670
Special ability...

17:18.800 --> 17:21.680
<b>Ultra Deduction</b>

17:19.220 --> 17:20.630
Ultra Deduction!

17:21.850 --> 17:26.270
<b>Who is Kamui?</b>

17:22.570 --> 17:24.690
<i>Who is Kamui?</i>

17:25.130 --> 17:29.140
<i>Kamui uses Fyodor and Nikolai as his pawns.</i>

17:29.140 --> 17:32.770
<i>That takes a capable, charismatic person.</i>

17:33.390 --> 17:37.080
<i>Given that they chose the Detective Agency 
as the victim of the false charge,</i>

17:37.080 --> 17:38.890
<i>they have some sort of connection to the Agency.</i>

17:38.890 --> 17:40.410
<i>Or they may be directly involved.</i>

17:40.410 --> 17:44.870
<b>Kamui made extraordinary profits from the series of terrorist attacks.</b>

17:41.080 --> 17:44.870
Kamui made extraordinary profits
from the series of terrorist attacks.

17:45.960 --> 17:47.920
<b>One man fits the description.</b>

17:50.540 --> 17:53.300
<b>His name...</b>

17:59.310 --> 18:00.770
<i>I have no proof...</i>

18:01.120 --> 18:02.510
<i>But it makes sense.</i>

18:02.770 --> 18:04.090
<i>But what's his motivation?</i>

18:04.740 --> 18:09.050
He must be a little lonely,
now that I've found my own path.

18:09.560 --> 18:11.240
<i>I see...</i>

18:11.240 --> 18:13.720
<i>So this is your path.</i>

18:17.380 --> 18:18.280
<i>What can I do?</i>

18:18.980 --> 18:21.420
<i>He's realized that I've realized.</i>

18:21.980 --> 18:23.540
<i>I only have a few seconds.</i>

18:30.590 --> 18:31.470
Rampo-san?

18:34.900 --> 18:36.080
A smoke flare?

18:41.370 --> 18:45.260
You may be guided by justice,
but I'm guided by the president.

18:46.120 --> 18:48.600
That's why I trust you, too.

18:49.710 --> 18:50.680
Atsushi...

18:52.340 --> 18:53.660
I'm sorry.

18:53.660 --> 18:54.640
I messed up.

19:01.130 --> 19:02.690
Run, Atsushi!

19:02.690 --> 19:04.320
You don't stand a chance!

19:05.220 --> 19:10.550
<i>That's the detective novel by Poe-san that
 Rampo-san keeps on him as an escape route.</i>

19:10.550 --> 19:12.130
And one more thing...

19:12.130 --> 19:15.110
Kamui's special ability 
increases his weapon's...

19:24.340 --> 19:27.340
So the boy saw through me.

19:27.880 --> 19:32.970
During my time as a military infiltrator,
they used to call me the hundred-faced man.

19:33.590 --> 19:34.680
I must be getting old.

19:35.240 --> 19:36.650
You're Kamui.

19:36.860 --> 19:38.530
Something like that.

19:38.530 --> 19:43.560
It's not healthy to be taking on 
a totally different personality.

19:43.990 --> 19:44.780
Though...

19:46.460 --> 19:48.700
I only need to keep it 
up for another six days.

19:48.950 --> 19:49.750
Why?!

19:49.750 --> 19:51.860
You're synonymous with justice.

19:51.860 --> 19:53.700
Weren't you the president's close friend?

19:53.700 --> 19:55.080
Close friend, huh?

19:56.290 --> 19:58.710
Yeah. He's my close friend, all right.

19:59.950 --> 20:03.940
But Fukuzawa has never
 been to a warzone.

20:06.260 --> 20:08.840
That's how our paths diverged.

20:08.840 --> 20:10.420
Forever.

20:12.430 --> 20:15.110
Never mind that. Are you sure, were-boy?

20:15.940 --> 20:19.820
The coast guard will side 
with me once we dock.

20:20.090 --> 20:24.640
You have two options right now:
to fight or to run.

20:25.160 --> 20:27.150
Neither will be easy.

20:27.460 --> 20:31.930
Now that you know who I am, 
I can't let you leave alive.

20:32.540 --> 20:36.130
I can at least simplify your 
circumstances for you.

20:36.420 --> 20:37.380
That's...

20:37.950 --> 20:39.390
The page.

20:39.670 --> 20:41.610
The reality amendment device.

20:41.610 --> 20:43.340
The root of all that's happening.

20:43.340 --> 20:46.600
Take it from me, and everything 
will return to normal.

20:46.600 --> 20:48.390
The Agency will be saved.

20:50.200 --> 20:52.150
The passengers have caught on.

20:52.790 --> 20:55.640
It won't be long before security arrives.

20:55.640 --> 20:57.090
<i>What do I do?</i>

20:57.090 --> 20:58.960
<i>If I win, everything will be solved.</i>

20:59.410 --> 21:03.360
<i>But if I lose, Rampo-san and I will die.</i>

21:03.570 --> 21:05.030
Run, Atsushi!

21:05.030 --> 21:06.650
You don't stand a chance!

21:07.090 --> 21:09.190
<i>But even if I run, he'll catch me.</i>

21:10.360 --> 21:11.320
<i>So...</i>

21:13.860 --> 21:16.920
<i>I can only make a way forward by fighting.</i>

21:17.830 --> 21:19.620
You've put on the face of a warrior.

21:20.000 --> 21:23.010
<i>More than anything, this man 
ruined the Detective Agency.</i>

21:23.010 --> 21:23.900
<i>I can't forgive him!</i>

21:24.190 --> 21:27.080
By the way, how will you 
fight with that leg?

21:31.620 --> 21:33.370
<i>When did he cut it?</i>

21:33.370 --> 21:35.040
Why are you surprised?

21:35.690 --> 21:38.390
The boy told you what my ability is.

21:40.400 --> 21:42.230
And one more thing...

21:42.230 --> 21:46.610
Kamui's special ability increases the power
of any weapon he uses a hundredfold.

21:48.500 --> 21:49.590
Get up.

21:49.590 --> 21:55.110
Compared to the ordeals in my autobiography, 
that isn't even a scrape.

21:59.680 --> 22:00.720
Ah.

22:01.110 --> 22:03.760
The tiger's regenerative ability.

22:03.760 --> 22:05.000
I'm impressed.

22:05.500 --> 22:09.980
Would your head grow back if I cut it off?

22:13.060 --> 22:18.520
<b><i>Fear</i></b>

22:13.420 --> 22:14.460
<i>I'm scared.</i>

22:16.010 --> 22:17.620
<i>I'm not afraid of the enemy.</i>

22:18.490 --> 22:20.390
<i>I'm not afraid of pain.</i>

22:23.030 --> 22:26.490
<b>I'm afraid</b>

22:23.040 --> 22:25.690
<i>I'm afraid of being alone.</i>

22:24.280 --> 22:26.490
<b>of being alone</b>

22:27.050 --> 22:29.910
<i>I was always alone in the orphanage.</i>

22:30.500 --> 22:34.310
<i>But now, I'm so afraid of loneliness.</i>

22:35.620 --> 22:39.500
The Detective Agency members were separated
because of the Decay of Angels incident.

22:39.500 --> 22:41.260
I thought I was alone.

22:45.100 --> 22:48.270
<i>But Kyouka-chan was beside me.</i>

22:48.990 --> 22:55.120
<i>And then, Francis, Ango-san, 
and Lucy-chan helped me.</i>

22:55.760 --> 22:58.740
<i>But now, I'm really alone.</i>

22:59.210 --> 23:02.730
<i>Somebody, anybody, please, 
fight alongside me.</i>

23:02.770 --> 23:06.400
<b>Somebody, anybody...</b>

23:06.670 --> 23:08.960
What's that noise on the 
other side of the deck?

23:08.960 --> 23:10.420
Why is there smoke?

23:12.020 --> 23:12.770
Let's go.

23:13.130 --> 23:14.660
We should call security.

23:22.630 --> 23:24.510
A smoke flare, huh?

23:32.950 --> 23:35.970
The impossible prophecy has come true.

23:35.970 --> 23:39.970
Next Episode         Episode 53
